NVIDIA's user-mode driver won't start without this object, so a sensor daemon
that couldn't start cost a guest CUDA and Vulkan and not just its readings. The
page now comes first and the daemon second. With no daemon the page stays empty,
which a guest reads as N/A.

The daemon can't hang a vCPU any more either, and if it dies its last readings
go with it. It runs with signals unblocked too, as it inherited a vCPU's mask.
